{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And do not touch anything that is theirs.</b> For if they come to save their property, they will descend to Sheol like them. And what it says, ״they go out and stand״ — they said in the Midrash: they were reviling and blaspheming. ״Going out״ and ״standing״ are said here, and ״going out״ and ״standing״ are said of Goliath, as it says (1 Samuel 17:16): ״ויצא איש הבינים״ etc., and the Philistine would draw near morning and evening and present himself (ויתיצב) forty days. Just as the ״going out״ and ״standing״ there were in blasphemy, so too here in blasphemy. Therefore Moses opened with ״hereby you shall know״ etc., ״if like the death of all men״ etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:14.448290838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}